From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3: a long press on an icon moves it, and nothing else

Two gestures were on one press and they got in each other's way, which is what
it feels like on the device ("很容易和长按移动冲突", 2026-10-20, V60). AOSP's
beginDragShared opens the shortcut popup and then arms the drag behind it, with
the popup's pre-drag condition: the drag does not begin until the popup is up
and the finger has moved past a threshold. On a panel where every frame of that
popup is an update, the first thing a long press does is spend several of them
drawing a menu the reader did not ask for.

And the menu is empty here. It holds an application's own shortcuts, which none
of the applications on this device declare; its notifications, which nothing
listens for; and widgets, which Launcher3Go turns off (GO_DISABLE_WIDGETS). So
what is left is one entry, and it is reachable anyway: a drag raises 移除,
应用信息 and 卸载 at the top of the screen (drop_target_bar_horz.xml), by the
gesture the reader has already started.

So the popup is not shown from here, and a long press drags at once. The popup
itself stays where AOSP put it: LauncherAccessibilityDelegate opens it too, and
that caller has no drag to fall back on.

diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/Workspace.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/Workspace.java
index 37ee6d7..20c77df 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/Workspace.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/Workspace.java
@@ -2179,15 +2179,22 @@ public class Workspace extends PagedView
             mDragSourceInternal = (ShortcutAndWidgetContainer) child.getParent();
         }
 
-        if (child instanceof BubbleTextView && !dragOptions.isAccessibleDrag) {
-            PopupContainerWithArrow popupContainer = PopupContainerWithArrow
-                    .showForIcon((BubbleTextView) child);
-            if (popupContainer != null) {
-                dragOptions.preDragCondition = popupContainer.createPreDragCondition();
-
-                mLauncher.getUserEventDispatcher().resetElapsedContainerMillis();
-            }
-        }
+        // PW3: a long press moves the icon, and nothing else. AOSP opens the
+        // shortcut popup here and arms the drag behind it, so the drag only
+        // begins once the popup is up and the finger has moved past the
+        // pre-drag threshold -- two gestures on one press, and on e-paper the
+        // popup is several panel updates before the first one answers.
+        //
+        // What the popup would offer is empty on this device: the applications
+        // here declare no shortcuts, widgets are off (GO_DISABLE_WIDGETS), and
+        // notifications are not listened for. Nothing is lost by not showing
+        // it: a drag raises 移除 / 应用信息 / 卸载 at the top of the screen
+        // (drop_target_bar_horz.xml), which is the same three things, reached
+        // by the gesture already under way.
+        //
+        // The popup itself is left where AOSP put it; accessibility still
+        // opens it (LauncherAccessibilityDelegate), which is the one caller
+        // that has no drag to fall back on.
 
         DragView dv = mDragController.startDrag(b, dragLayerX, dragLayerY, source,
                 dragObject, dragVisualizeOffset, dragRect, scale, dragOptions);
